+Feature: S010 portable cohort feature-flag rehearsal
learning/S010/specification.feature:2: trailing whitespace.
+  Training rehearsal - synthetic data - not a live Azure result
learning/S010/specification.feature:3: trailing whitespace.
+  Source: README.md S010; backlog.md D-S010; kanban.md A-S010 (SOURCE)
learning/S010/specification.feature:4: trailing whitespace.
+  Kano unit: A-S010, frozen S; owner: worker-A-S010
learning/S010/specification.feature:5: trailing whitespace.
+  Compatible code is already present in one synthetic deployment.
learning/S010/specification.feature:6: trailing whitespace.
+  Flag changes are behavior changes, not deployment migration or authorization.
learning/S010/specification.feature:7: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S010/specification.feature:8: trailing whitespace.
+  Scenario: Observe baseline, cohort activation, and reversal
learning/S010/specification.feature:9: trailing whitespace.
+    Given two pilot and two control synthetic sessions use config v1 and state v1
learning/S010/specification.feature:10: trailing whitespace.
+    When I observe their baseline journeys
learning/S010/specification.feature:11: trailing whitespace.
+    And enable the feature for the pilot cohort using config v1
learning/S010/specification.feature:12: trailing whitespace.
+    And observe the same four journeys
learning/S010/specification.feature:13: trailing whitespace.
+    Then only the pilot sessions use enhanced behavior
learning/S010/specification.feature:14: trailing whitespace.
+    And all session tokens, cart identifiers, and prior data remain intact
learning/S010/specification.feature:15: trailing whitespace.
+    When I revert the flag to off and observe again
learning/S010/specification.feature:16: trailing whitespace.
+    Then all four sessions return to standard behavior on the same deployment
learning/S010/specification.feature:17: trailing whitespace.
+    And each successful journey has exactly one synthetic cart effect
learning/S010/specification.feature:18: trailing whitespace.
+    And the readable verdict passes only this synthetic flag-continuity exercise
learning/S010/specification.feature:19: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S010/specification.feature:20: trailing whitespace.
+  Scenario Outline: Reject incompatible assumptions before flag publication
learning/S010/specification.feature:21: trailing whitespace.
+    Given the declared already-deployed code supports config v1 and state v1 only
learning/S010/specification.feature:22: trailing whitespace.
+    And <condition>
learning/S010/specification.feature:23: trailing whitespace.
+    When I attempt to enable the cohort flag
learning/S010/specification.feature:24: trailing whitespace.
+    Then the compatibility guard rejects publication without changing the flag
learning/S010/specification.feature:25: trailing whitespace.
+    And the trace identifies <reason>
learning/S010/specification.feature:26: trailing whitespace.
+    And the verdict says guarded, not successful migration
learning/S010/specification.feature:27: trailing whitespace.
+    Examples:
learning/S010/specification.feature:28: trailing whitespace.
+      | condition                         | reason                     |
learning/S010/specification.feature:29: trailing whitespace.
+      | proposed configuration is v2       | CONFIG_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED |
learning/S010/specification.feature:30: trailing whitespace.
+      | a synthetic session has state v2   | STATE_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED  |
learning/S010/specification.feature:31: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S010/specification.feature:32: trailing whitespace.
+  Scenario: Reversal cannot conceal an earlier interruption
learning/S010/specification.feature:33: trailing whitespace.
+    Given the pilot flag has been enabled with compatible configuration
learning/S010/specification.feature:34: trailing whitespace.
+    When I deliberately inject state v2 for pilot-1 and observe journeys
learning/S010/specification.feature:35: trailing whitespace.
+    Then pilot-1 is interrupted without a synthetic write
learning/S010/specification.feature:36: trailing whitespace.
+    And other compatible sessions continue
learning/S010/specification.feature:37: trailing whitespace.
+    When I revert the flag and observe again
learning/S010/specification.feature:38: trailing whitespace.
+    Then the incompatible state remains incompatible
learning/S010/specification.feature:39: trailing whitespace.
+    When I restore the compatible state fixture and observe again
learning/S010/specification.feature:40: trailing whitespace.
+    Then later journeys can continue with preserved session and cart data
learning/S010/specification.feature:41: trailing whitespace.
+    But earlier interrupted attempts remain in the denominator and failing verdict
learning/S010/specification.feature:42: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S010/specification.feature:43: trailing whitespace.
+  Scenario: Strict inputs and unsupported operations fail explicitly
learning/S010/specification.feature:44: trailing whitespace.
+    When an event is malformed JSON or has wrong primitive types or extra fields
learning/S010/specification.feature:45: trailing whitespace.
+    Or it names an unknown cohort, client, fixture version, operation, or run version
learning/S010/specification.feature:46: trailing whitespace.
+    Then an explicit coded input error is returned without changing the run
learning/S010/specification.feature:47: trailing whitespace.
+    And strings are never coerced into booleans or version numbers
learning/S010/specification.feature:48: trailing whitespace.
+    And no management, network, identity, native, or deployment action is available
learning/S010/specification.feature:49: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S010/specification.feature:50: trailing whitespace.
+  Scenario: Determinism and observation requirements
learning/S010/specification.feature:51: trailing whitespace.
+    Given the same explicit bounded synthetic event sequence
learning/S010/specification.feature:52: trailing whitespace.
+    Then replay produces identical trace, sessions, counts, and verdict
learning/S010/specification.feature:53: trailing whitespace.
+    And merely changing the desired flag without observations cannot pass
learning/S010/specification.feature:54: trailing whitespace.
+    And neither a missing baseline nor a missing post-reversal observation can pass
learning/S010/specification.feature:55: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S010/specification.feature:56: trailing whitespace.
+  Scenario: Keyboard operation, safe rendering, CSP, and reset
learning/S010/specification.feature:57: trailing whitespace.
+    Given I open index.html directly in a real isolated browser
learning/S010/specification.feature:58: trailing whitespace.
+    Then the exact training banner and native-proof limits are prominent
learning/S010/specification.feature:59: trailing whitespace.
+    And every input has a label and every action is keyboard operable
learning/S010/specification.feature:60: trailing whitespace.
+    And no control named or identified as reset shadows form.reset
learning/S010/specification.feature:61: trailing whitespace.
+    When I submit a valid explicit synthetic event using the keyboard
learning/S010/specification.feature:62: trailing whitespace.
+    Then the actual DOM shows the resulting trace and readable verdict
learning/S010/specification.feature:63: trailing whitespace.
+    When I submit malformed input or hostile markup
learning/S010/specification.feature:64: trailing whitespace.
+    Then an accessible error is shown as text without executing markup
learning/S010/specification.feature:65: trailing whitespace.
+    When I reset the rehearsal
learning/S010/specification.feature:66: trailing whitespace.
+    Then a fresh baseline run starts and prior results are visibly archived in memory
learning/S010/specification.feature:67: trailing whitespace.
+    And the native form reset method still works
learning/S010/specification.feature:68: trailing whitespace.
+    And CSP blocks inline code and outbound connections
